# Env
#
# The negations MUST come after `.env.*`, not before it: later patterns win, so
# a `!.env.example` above the broad rule is silently overridden — which is how
# the sample file the README tells you to copy went missing from the repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.test

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
/.svelte-kit
/build
dist/
out/
.output
.cache/
.netlify
.vercel
.wrangler
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# Assistant tooling state, not source.
#
# Local scratch belonging to the agent tooling that has been run against this
# repo — vector stores, neural caches, policy hashes. It is per-machine, it
# churns on every session, and it was 5.8 MB of the repository.
#
# `.claude` is a glob and not a directory for one reason: git does not descend
# into an excluded DIRECTORY, so `.claude/` followed by a negation would keep
# ignoring launch.json however the negation is written. `.claude/*` leaves git
# walking the directory, and the later pattern wins — the same ordering rule
# as the .env block at the top of this file.
#
# launch.json is the dev-server definition. That is real project
# configuration and belongs in the repository.
.claude-flow/
.swarm/
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json
agentdb.rvf
agentdb.rvf.idmap.json
ruvector.db
